    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0165" n="81" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg81"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/3734</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-22T14:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2147. Your 3703, June 19, 3 p.m. Request Spanish Embassy, Berlin, to inform
                    German Government that in view of its acceptance in principle of this
                    Government’s proposal that a conference be held in Berne concerning a proposed
                    agreement regarding the maintenance, treatment, and exchange of prisoners of war
                    of the two countries, this Government proposes that such a conference be held at
                    Berne on August 5, 1918.</p>
                <p>Further request Spanish Embassy to ascertain at earliest possible moment whether
                    this date is acceptable to German Government, and state that upon the receipt of
                    the acceptance this Government will <pb facs="0166" n="82" xml:id="pg82"/> make
                    known to the German Government the delegates whom it proposes sending to the
                    conference and will be ready to receive a similar statement on the part of the
                    German Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
